## Sources & references

The four-lever framing in this article (operations, supply chain, service, quality) is a synthesis of standard operations management literature, particularly Wallace Hopp and Mark Spearman's *Factory Physics* (3rd ed., 2008) for the operations-as-systems view, James Womack and Daniel Jones's *Lean Thinking* (1996) for the waste-elimination tradition, and the broader Six Sigma / TPS body of work. Reichheld and Sasser's foundational [*Zero Defections: Quality Comes to Services*](https://hbr.org/1990/09/zero-defections-quality-comes-to-services) (Harvard Business Review, 1990) is the canonical case for customer-retention economics; the math on avoided CAC traces back to this and the SaaS-era updates by David Skok. Malaysian SME margin and labour cost data referenced informally draws on SME Corp Malaysia and Department of Statistics Malaysia (DOSM) reports, which the reader should verify before using as benchmarks.
